                      GIS = c(rep("FOREST",3),rep("NA",5),rep("COAST",3),rep("NA",4),rep("FOREST",7),rep("NA",8)))
str(example) # shows that IDs, trip, and GIS are all factors.

The GIS column by trip should look like:
example$GIStrip <- c(rep("MIXED",15),rep("FOREST",15),rep("MIXED",15),rep("FOREST",15))

I've tried to create this code using piping with if_else, ifelse, and coercing column GIS to a character. None of them yield the (untidy) information I need.

Using if_else and GIS as a factor:
