  arrange(IDs, timestamp) %>%
  group_by(IDs, trip) %>%
  mutate(GIStrip = ifelse(n_distinct(GIS, na.rm = TRUE) > 1, "MIXED", GIS))

If I change the class of GIS to a character, I get the same result with both if_else and ifelse, respectively. Any ideas re: how to get the GIS column I'd like?

